    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n22017" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">imprĕcātĭo</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">inpr-</span></b> ),
			ōnis, f.
		imprecor, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>an invoking of evil</i>, <i>imprecation</i> (postAug.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">exsecraris illum et caput sanctum tibi dira
					imprecatione defigis,</span>”
				<i>curse</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Sen. Ben. 6, 35, 1</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">id. Ep. 94, 52</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">imprecationes nefariae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Amm. 29, 1, 25</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dira,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					5, 8, 8, § 45</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> In
			late Lat., in a good sense, a <i>prayer</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pontificis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hier. Ep. 130</span></i>
			, n. 2.</div>
